\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces BioRED, BioCreative VIII test set: 16{,}606 sentence-level candidates from 400 abstracts, $0.463$ positive, 538 from sentences naming two concepts. Headline rows repeat Table~\ref  {tab:main}. AUPRC is the per-seed mean $\pm $ standard deviation over three seeds (columns by concept count: three-checkpoint ensembles); F1 is at the pre-specified threshold (mean of the checkpoints' development thresholds), the teacher's at its greedy answer. EP F1 is BioRED's document-level entity-pair F1, a pair scoring the maximum over the sentences that co-mention it. On the teacher's sample the trained models' three-checkpoint ensembles score $0.757$ and $0.860$. Pair-conditioned against sentence-level: 2{,}642 items fixed, 1{,}064 broken (McNemar $p = 5.9\times 10^{-148}$).\relax }}{14}{table.caption.39}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:biored}{{5}{14}{BioRED, BioCreative VIII test set: 16{,}606 sentence-level candidates from 400 abstracts, $0.463$ positive, 538 from sentences naming two concepts. Headline rows repeat Table~\ref {tab:main}. AUPRC is the per-seed mean $\pm $ standard deviation over three seeds (columns by concept count: three-checkpoint ensembles); F1 is at the pre-specified threshold (mean of the checkpoints' development thresholds), the teacher's at its greedy answer. EP F1 is BioRED's document-level entity-pair F1, a pair scoring the maximum over the sentences that co-mention it. On the teacher's sample the trained models' three-checkpoint ensembles score $0.757$ and $0.860$. Pair-conditioned against sentence-level: 2{,}642 items fixed, 1{,}064 broken (McNemar $p = 5.9\times 10^{-148}$).\relax }{table.caption.39}{}}
