\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces AUPRC of zero-shot Qwen3 \citep  {qwen2025technical} by size, asked the three questions of Appendix~\ref  {app:prompts} (4-bit builds served locally, thinking disabled; the triple question in both argument orders, maxed). 30B-A3B is a mixture of experts with 3B active parameters; Qwen3.5-122B, a later release, is a mixture of experts with 8 of 256 experts active per token, run partly on the CPU. Base rates $0.574$ and $0.476$. Last row: the trained three-checkpoint ensembles on the same rows. $^\dagger $On the first 1{,}000 candidates of the sample (base rate $0.442$), where the 32B model scores $0.527$ and $0.796$ and the trained models $0.714$ and $0.841$.\relax }}{15}{table.caption.40}\protected@file@percent }
