\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces The three formulations under the encoders that were scored on test, recipe otherwise that of \S  \ref  {sec:verifier}: AUPRC and EP F1 (sentence-level/pair-conditioned) as per-seed means over three seeds, and block-held-out F1 of three-checkpoint ensembles. BiomedBERT-large was not trained on the biodiversity arms (Appendix~\ref  {sec:negative}). Against the base encoder's model of the same format, BioLinkBERT's pair-conditioned model fixes 621 BioRED items and breaks 537 (McNemar $p = 0.015$) and on ours 19 and 32 ($p = 0.093$); its sentence-level model on ours, 42 and 20 ($p = 0.0077$). No BioLinkBERT-large model differs significantly from the base encoder's on ours ($p \ge 0.23$).\relax }}{16}{table.caption.43}\protected@file@percent }
